1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,604
(Fukuko) Kakizaki-kun Eternal Boys Don't Quit NOTE Eternal Boys

2
00:00:03,604 --> 00:00:06,440
That's why I won't be performing live anymore.

3
00:00:08,275 --> 00:00:14,014
Haven't you heard? (Yamanaka) Ah, what do you mean?

4
00:00:37,037 --> 00:00:39,139
What do you mean by quitting?

5
00:00:42,209 --> 00:00:44,211
(Kakizaki) Thank you

6
00:00:44,211 --> 00:00:47,681
Why don't you tell Nikolai and the president and not us?

7
00:00:47,681 --> 00:00:50,517
Revenge live, what should we do?

8
00:00:50,517 --> 00:00:53,820
I'm not going out anymore, don't kid yourself!

9
00:00:53,820 --> 00:00:58,158
(Sanada) I'm home (Asai) Chissu NOTE Sanada

10
00:00:58,158 --> 00:01:01,595
(Kakizaki) Sorry, I have to go to work (Imagawa) Huh?

11
00:01:01,595 --> 00:01:06,400
To Kakizaki, was eternal boy such a light thing?

12
00:01:08,969 --> 00:01:15,809
♬～

13
00:01:15,809 --> 00:01:17,945
what happened? What… what?

14
00:01:21,181 --> 00:01:24,918
Kuuu

15
00:01:24,918 --> 00:01:30,023
Well, I guess you can make more money as a host.

16
00:01:30,023 --> 00:01:35,729
(Ishida) Or maybe Kakizaki-san is popular now that he has a girlfriend.

17
00:01:35,729 --> 00:01:47,241
Ha, I've hated that guy for a long time.

18
00:01:47,241 --> 00:01:51,044
Hey... Mr. Yamanaka, you've been drinking a little too much.

19
00:01:53,180 --> 00:01:56,350
Mr. Kakizaki

20
00:01:56,350 --> 00:02:00,187
You don't care about us.

21
00:02:00,187 --> 00:02:04,992
We were... abandoned.

22
00:02:04,992 --> 00:02:09,062
(cry)

23
00:02:12,499 --> 00:02:15,969
Why didn't you tell those kids?

24
00:02:15,969 --> 00:02:21,008
I just didn't have the timing.

25
00:02:21,008 --> 00:02:23,644
Maybe you're scared?

26
00:02:25,512 --> 00:02:27,514
no…

27
00:02:30,083 --> 00:02:33,053
Something has changed, hasn't it?

28
00:02:36,590 --> 00:02:42,329
Since we've known each other for a long time, I can easily tell if it's a lie.

29
00:02:42,329 --> 00:02:50,103
But even though we've known each other for a long time, lately we've been seeing each other for the first time.

30
00:02:53,874 --> 00:02:58,178
What is your calling?

31
00:03:02,683 --> 00:03:06,353
Kakizaki! you…

32
00:03:10,691 --> 00:03:13,126
Talking in your sleep...

33
00:03:15,863 --> 00:03:18,265
toilet…

34
00:03:48,896 --> 00:03:52,833
I'm going to catch a cold, Kakizaki-san.

35
00:04:01,542 --> 00:04:03,544
“Again”? NOTE AGAIN

36
00:04:21,862 --> 00:04:24,264
good night

37
00:04:28,135 --> 00:04:34,374
Mr. Kakizaki, I wonder if he won't come again? Leave that guy alone.

38
00:04:34,374 --> 00:04:39,012
I don't feel well. Why did you come here?

39
00:04:39,012 --> 00:04:41,982
The president's favorite Kakizaki is no longer there.

40
00:04:41,982 --> 00:04:46,753
I brought you a present.

41
00:04:46,753 --> 00:04:48,755
what? that

42
00:04:50,490 --> 00:04:53,794
Is it really a new song?

43
00:04:53,794 --> 00:04:58,765
(Ishida) Those are good lyrics, yeah, yeah.

44
00:04:58,765 --> 00:05:01,401
feel the love for the group

45
00:05:02,736 --> 00:05:16,316
♬～

46
00:05:16,316 --> 00:05:19,353
Where are you going at this hour?

47
00:05:22,155 --> 00:05:24,157
Where is Kakizaki?

48
00:05:25,726 --> 00:05:28,462
I'll go to the store and ask.

49
00:05:30,797 --> 00:05:34,001
But that store...

50
00:05:43,010 --> 00:05:48,415
♬～

51
00:05:48,415 --> 00:05:51,351
(Host) Welcome. This is my first time...

52
00:05:51,351 --> 00:05:53,787
Yes, we will guide you through the system.

53
00:05:53,787 --> 00:05:56,823
There are 3 plans... It's the cheapest.

54
00:05:56,823 --> 00:05:59,760
Please click here.

55
00:06:00,761 --> 00:06:03,897
(Host) Cheers to Sana-chan's first host club!

56
00:06:03,897 --> 00:06:07,734
(Hosts) Good! Okay, okay...

57
00:06:07,734 --> 00:06:09,903
(Hosts) Gui Gui Gui Gui Okay.

58
00:06:09,903 --> 00:06:14,708
Gui Gui Gui Gui Okay, Gui Gui Gui Gui Okay, Gui Gui

59
00:06:14,708 --> 00:06:18,712
Yes!

60
00:06:18,712 --> 00:06:21,515
Huh, Sana-chan, are you feeling nervous today?

61
00:06:21,515 --> 00:06:24,418
Yes haha, that's cute

62
00:06:24,418 --> 00:06:27,120
Huh... Ah, sorry, I need to go to the bathroom.

63
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:32,492
Cute What else? (Emi) Other than that, there are also rabbits.

64
00:06:32,492 --> 00:06:34,494
rabbit? Sorry

65
00:06:34,494 --> 00:06:36,496
Yeah, yeah, find it, okay?

66
00:06:36,496 --> 00:06:38,498
But here... did you notice?

67
00:06:38,498 --> 00:06:40,501
(Kakizaki) Hmm, cute (Emi) Hehehe

68
00:06:40,501 --> 00:06:43,470
That's why I put on a bear (Kakizaki) It's true, it's a bear.

69
00:06:43,470 --> 00:06:46,907
(Emi) Yeah, so I made it into a rabbit.

70
00:06:46,907 --> 00:06:49,510
(Kakizaki) That's true, it's cute.

71
00:06:49,510 --> 00:06:52,446
The other day, I went to a really stylish cafe.

72
00:06:52,446 --> 00:06:54,448
I think Emi will love it.

73
00:06:54,448 --> 00:06:56,617
Will you look at it? Wait, what? this

74
00:06:56,617 --> 00:06:59,620
Oh, wait... No, Emi-chan, give it back.

75
00:06:59,620 --> 00:07:03,857
No, no, give it back (Emi) Are there any lyrics?

76
00:07:03,857 --> 00:07:05,859
No, what? Tell me

77
00:07:05,859 --> 00:07:07,861
Besides, you went on a trip recently, right?

78
00:07:07,861 --> 00:07:09,863
(Emi) Eh, how do you know? (Kakizaki) I saw it in Korea.

79
00:07:09,863 --> 00:07:11,865
It looked like a lot of fun (Emi) Yeah?

80
00:07:11,865 --> 00:07:13,867
(Kakizaki) Did you eat a lot? (Emi) I ate a lot.

81
00:07:16,737 --> 00:07:18,739
Sanada…

82
00:07:21,141 --> 00:07:23,143
Thank you for your hard work

83
00:07:25,746 --> 00:07:27,748
Good job

84
00:07:31,018 --> 00:07:36,623
Mr. Kakizaki, do you want to become a lyricist?

85
00:07:36,623 --> 00:07:42,129
Huh? Why didn't you tell me?

86
00:07:45,165 --> 00:07:51,872
Is it a secret because you're the host?

87
00:07:51,872 --> 00:07:58,212
Yeah, I don't have the right to dream.

88
00:07:58,212 --> 00:08:04,084
Because I chose a job that makes my dreams come true.

89
00:08:04,084 --> 00:08:10,524
I see, Kakizaki-san is always cool.

90
00:08:19,132 --> 00:08:26,206
Sorry, I tried to be cool.

91
00:08:26,206 --> 00:08:31,345
I've been lying to everyone all the time

92
00:08:31,345 --> 00:08:36,717
Actually, I don't want to be an idol.

93
00:08:36,717 --> 00:08:43,290
As a lyricist, I would like to produce idols.

94
00:08:43,290 --> 00:08:53,567
But I'm actually a coward because I'm afraid of failing.

95
00:08:53,567 --> 00:08:55,569
It's uncool

96
00:08:58,272 --> 00:09:00,274
sorry…

97
00:09:03,744 --> 00:09:08,315
There's nothing uncool about that, right?

98
00:09:12,819 --> 00:09:15,489
Because what attracts people

99
00:09:15,489 --> 00:09:22,696
I'm sure there's something beyond "still"

100
00:09:28,101 --> 00:09:30,704
Be careful of the angle, isn't it too high? that

101
00:09:30,704 --> 00:09:33,540
Yeah, about this much

102
00:09:33,540 --> 00:09:36,710
Sorry I'm late

103
00:09:38,879 --> 00:09:48,021
What did you come here for now? I'm sorry...

104
00:09:48,021 --> 00:09:52,259
Go home with Kakizaki, I don't want to sing this song

105
00:09:52,259 --> 00:09:57,431
Mr. Yamanaka... these wonderful lyrics

106
00:09:57,431 --> 00:10:01,034
This can only be made by someone who loves Eternal Shonen.

107
00:10:01,034 --> 00:10:06,073
These are sacred lyrics full of love.

108
00:10:06,073 --> 00:10:12,513
I don't want to be tainted by someone who abandoned the group.

109
00:10:12,513 --> 00:10:15,048
Hehehehe

110
00:10:15,048 --> 00:10:18,619
What? Sanada, there's nothing wrong with that.

111
00:10:18,619 --> 00:10:24,258
Yamanaka-san, who do you think wrote these lyrics?

112
00:10:24,258 --> 00:10:31,765
Who must have had such great love...

113
00:10:35,502 --> 00:10:40,974
It's Kakizaki-san (Imagawa/Asai) Yeah!

114
00:10:40,974 --> 00:10:45,179
Sorry for keeping it a secret

115
00:10:45,179 --> 00:10:50,918
I don't want to quit being a forever boy.

116
00:10:50,918 --> 00:10:59,226
Actually, I want to work as a lyricist and produce.

117
00:10:59,226 --> 00:11:03,997
Wow, that's amazing. (Asai) Kakizaki-san, are you a genius?

118
00:11:03,997 --> 00:11:08,335
Please let me know sooner

119
00:11:08,335 --> 00:11:10,337
What about Mr. Yamanaka?

120
00:11:10,337 --> 00:11:17,344
♬～

121
00:11:17,344 --> 00:11:22,115
Okay, but is there a condition?

122
00:11:22,115 --> 00:11:26,353
Finally, go to the last live.

123
00:11:26,353 --> 00:11:33,060
Would you like to sing "Again" with me?

124
00:11:33,060 --> 00:11:38,031
You wrote it, so take responsibility and sing it.

125
00:11:38,031 --> 00:11:42,503
Mr. Yamanaka: Whenever I go to a public bath these days, I find myself singing “Again” all the time.

126
00:11:42,503 --> 00:11:44,505
You... you're tone deaf.

127
00:11:44,505 --> 00:11:47,040
That's too loud (Imagawa) hahahaha

128
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:49,042
Yamanaka-san, are you really happy?

129
00:11:49,042 --> 00:11:53,914
Okay, let's practice now. Don't be so loud. Don't be tone deaf.

130
00:11:53,914 --> 00:11:56,316
(Asai) Even though the sounds don't match at all, they match.

131
00:11:57,317 --> 00:12:01,021
Manpuku Entertainment is over and Eternal Shonen is disbanded.

132
00:12:01,021 --> 00:12:03,190
Why do people give up so easily?

133
00:12:03,190 --> 00:12:05,993
I don't want to disband, I want to be an idol with everyone.
